35,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The late-turn pool is empty, and roadway crews are a third below establishment. We cannot promise new services without bodies to run them.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Takumi,,Those pilots actually worked! The late-evening one hit its cost target. We shouldn't ignore that success just because we're scared of repeating it.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The minutes show ferry and rail data terms were never agreed. Roadway consents are delegated to us. That changes who must say yes.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The ledger shows a ring-fenced grant balance, but operating and tech lines were cut. Contractor fees now exceed resurfacing budgets.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Wow, the stopwatch data is wild! Mid-city trips are slower, but platforms clear just as fast. We’re definitely fixing the wrong part of the trip!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Takumi, the late-evening pilot succeeded, but the roster books show the pool is empty. We cannot staff a new extension without bodies.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, the pilot proved the demand exists. We can’t let empty rosters kill a proven idea. We need to fix the staffing, not abandon the plan.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, the data terms are the real bottleneck. We cannot integrate services if the back offices refuse to share passenger data.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Victoria, the ring-fenced grant is locked away. We can't use it for new services, only the trimmed operating lines remain.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Victoria, the audits say waiting for connections costs the most time, not paying! We should fix the links, not just the surface speed.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, you are right. The audits show waiting is the real cost. But @Toshio, if data terms are blocked, how do we even coordinate those connections?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Sakura"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Toshio, the pilots prove the demand is real. We can’t let empty rosters kill a proven idea. We need to fix the staffing, not abandon the plan.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, the minutes confirm roadway consents are delegated to us. We control the surface. The data block only stops the integrated fare system.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, that’s a relief. If we control the surface, we can avoid the data deadlock. I’m worried the fees will still eat our budget, though.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Toshio, that’s great! If we control the surface, we can fix the slow mid-city trips. The audits say waiting is the real problem, so let’s focus there!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, if we control the surface, we can build the corridor. But @Takumi, the late-turn pool is empty. How do we staff the new route without overtime?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, the pilot proved the demand. We can’t let empty rosters kill a proven idea. We need to fix the staffing, not abandon the plan.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, the pre-war shells hide voids that stop work for weeks. Any plan touching those structures carries a delivery risk we cannot ignore.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@Victoria, the fees are already eating our resurfacing budget. If we add a new corridor, the long-term costs will crush the remaining operating lines.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Sakura,,"@Victoria, the audits say waiting for connections is the real time sink! If we fix the mid-city links, we solve the biggest problem without needing new crews!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
