60,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"@Takumi, the late-turn pool is empty. Plan B requires new rosters we simply do not have. We cannot staff an extension without bodies.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Victoria"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Victoria: @Takumi, the late-turn pool is empty. Plan B requires new rosters we simply do not have. We cannot staff an extension without bodies.""}]}"
61,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, the pilot proved the demand! We can’t let empty rosters kill a proven idea. We need to fix the staffing, not abandon the plan.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, Plan C is a trap. The pre-war shells hide voids that stop work for weeks. I cannot trust any delivery date for those structures.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, I agree. Plan C’s hidden voids are a nightmare. But Plan D’s contractor fees are already crushing our resurfacing budget.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"@Victoria, the audits say waiting for connections is the real time sink! Plan A fixes the mid-city links, solving the biggest problem without needing new crews!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, I agree. Plan A uses existing surface control. @Daisuke, does the ring-fenced grant cover the lane construction, or is that a new operating cost?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Sakura"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, the old lane-priority stretches got reverted to mixed traffic. Plan A risks the same failure unless we lock in the dedicated lanes permanently.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, the reversion proves the commitment was weak. If we secure the consents now, the lanes hold. The ground risk is manageable.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Victoria, the grant is ring-fenced for construction, so it covers the lanes. But the operating subsidy is already cut, so running it will strain us.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Takumi, that’s a scary thought! But @Toshio, if we lock the lanes, it works. Plan A fixes the waiting, which is the real problem!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Daisuke, if the grant covers construction, Plan A is viable. @Takumi, we must secure permanent lane consents to prevent reversion. I support A.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, I agree. The pilots proved the demand, but the accessibility records show we must lock the lanes permanently. I support Plan A.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, I support Plan A. The roadway consents are delegated to us, so we control the surface. The pre-war voids do not threaten this route.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Victoria, I support Plan A. The grant covers the lanes, and we avoid the data deadlock. It is the only option that fits our remaining budget.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Victoria, I support Plan A too! The stopwatch data proves it fixes the real waiting problem. Let’s lock those lanes in!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I support Plan A. It fits our staffing reality and budget. Let us forward it to the board.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"I support Plan A. The pilots proved the demand, and locking the lanes prevents the old mistakes. Let's send it to the board.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"I support Plan A. We control the surface consents, avoiding the pre-war ground risks. It is the only viable path forward.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I support Plan A. The grant covers the lanes, and we avoid the data deadlock. It is the only option that fits our remaining budget.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Sakura,,I support Plan A! The stopwatch data proves it fixes the real waiting problem. Let’s lock those lanes in and send it to the board!,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
